CM_ BO_ 1536 "PC to all boards. Only SCAN (MsgType 1) is accepted in broadcast.";
CM_ BO_ 1605 "PC to Dashboard (ESP32-S3): commands. MsgType 1 SCAN, 16 BEGIN, 17 CRC, 18 BLOCK_END, 19 FINISH, 20 ABORT, 21 ENTER_BOOT, 32 DETAILS, 33 REBOOT, 34 IDENTIFY, 35 ROLLBACK, 48 PARAM_READ, 49 PARAM_WRITE, 50 PARAM_SAVE, 51 PARAM_RESET.";
CM_ BO_ 1733 "Dashboard (ESP32-S3) to PC: heartbeat, scan answers (INFO_A, INFO_B), update answers, details (DETAIL_A..PART_B), action answer and parameter answers.";
CM_ SG_ 1733 HwRevision "Hardware revision as an ASCII letter (65 = A, 66 = B).";
CM_ SG_ 1733 AckBlock "Number of the block confirmed (or refused) by the board.";
CM_ BO_ 1349 "Dashboard (ESP32-S3) to PC: sensor value, sent by the board by itself every 100 ms (20..500 ms). No command byte. Not sent during a firmware update.";
CM_ SG_ 1349 SensorValue "Value in the unit of the gauge (tenths on the bus). -0.1 (FF FF) = no valid value yet.";
CM_ SG_ 1349 SensorMv "Voltage at the connector.";
CM_ SG_ 1349 FlagFault "Sensor in fault (wire cut, short to ground, short to 5 V). All the alarms are off.";
CM_ SG_ 1349 FrameCounter "Grows at every frame (0..255): it stops if the board stops.";
CM_ SG_ 1733 TempC "-128 = not available.";
CM_ SG_ 1733 PartFlags "bit0 = running now, bit1 = starts at next boot, bit2 = valid image found.";
CM_ SG_ 1733 PartAddr "Address in units of 64 KB.";
CM_ SG_ 1733 PartSize "Size in units of 64 KB.";
CM_ SG_ 1733 PartVerMajor "255 = no firmware in the slot.";
CM_ SG_ 1733 GitDirty "1 = the firmware was built with uncommitted changes.";
CM_ SG_ 1733 ValValue "Value of the parameter, 4 bytes little endian. Numbers with decimals are multiplied by 10.";
CM_ SG_ 1605 WriteValue "New value of the parameter, 4 bytes little endian. Numbers with decimals are multiplied by 10.";
CM_ BO_ 1861 "File data for Dashboard (ESP32-S3): 8 raw bytes per frame, 32 frames per block of 256 bytes.";
CM_ BO_ 1584 "PC to PDM Anteriore (STM32): commands. MsgType 1 SCAN, 16 BEGIN, 17 CRC, 18 BLOCK_END, 19 FINISH, 20 ABORT, 21 ENTER_BOOT.";
CM_ BO_ 1712 "PDM Anteriore (STM32) to PC: heartbeat, scan answers (INFO_A, INFO_B) and update answers.";
CM_ SG_ 1712 HwRevision "Hardware revision as an ASCII letter (65 = A, 66 = B).";
CM_ SG_ 1712 AckBlock "Number of the block confirmed (or refused) by the board.";
CM_ BO_ 1840 "File data for PDM Anteriore (STM32): 8 raw bytes per frame, 32 frames per block of 256 bytes.";
CM_ BO_ 1585 "PC to PDM Posteriore (STM32): commands. MsgType 1 SCAN, 16 BEGIN, 17 CRC, 18 BLOCK_END, 19 FINISH, 20 ABORT, 21 ENTER_BOOT.";
CM_ BO_ 1713 "PDM Posteriore (STM32) to PC: heartbeat, scan answers (INFO_A, INFO_B) and update answers.";
CM_ SG_ 1713 HwRevision "Hardware revision as an ASCII letter (65 = A, 66 = B).";
CM_ SG_ 1713 AckBlock "Number of the block confirmed (or refused) by the board.";
CM_ BO_ 1841 "File data for PDM Posteriore (STM32): 8 raw bytes per frame, 32 frames per block of 256 bytes.";
CM_ BO_ 1569 "PC to Tastierino: commands. MsgType 1 SCAN, 16 BEGIN, 17 CRC, 18 BLOCK_END, 19 FINISH, 20 ABORT, 21 ENTER_BOOT.";
CM_ BO_ 1697 "Tastierino to PC: heartbeat, scan answers (INFO_A, INFO_B) and update answers.";
CM_ SG_ 1697 HwRevision "Hardware revision as an ASCII letter (65 = A, 66 = B).";
CM_ SG_ 1697 AckBlock "Number of the block confirmed (or refused) by the board.";
